NEXTGENDRIVE Native Bluetooth
The complete public Windows installer bundles Python/Tk, a PyInstaller bootloader, official ADB, project/AOSP Bluetooth components and non-payload ZIP reconstruction metadata. Separate runtime and ADB notices are supplied in third-party-licenses; AOSP-NOTICE.txt is retained. Project code remains Apache-2.0. OEM library payloads and Settings entry payloads are read only from the owner's radio and are not bundled.
The AVRCP extension headers in src/android-app/jni/ngd_avrcp_legacy retain their Android Open Source Project and Linux Foundation copyright and Apache-2.0 notices. See docs/PROVENANCE.md for the upstream reference.
Project additions: NEXTGENDRIVE contributors, 2026. Apache License 2.0.
Contains source derived from the Android Open Source Project; retain individual copyright headers and licenses/AOSP-NOTICE.txt.
The source license does not claim ownership of OEM runtime libraries, Settings APK, Audi/Qualcomm/Microsoft trademarks or private per-device data. Complete locally reconstructed OEM payloads are excluded from Git. Public project components and recipes are recorded in profiles/public-components-20261020.json.

The charging-to-hotspot companion is project source under Apache-2.0. The included APK is built from project code and contains no OEM runtime libraries. User-provided photographs in docs/images are illustrative assets, separate from the source-code licence.
